Accepted deviation: verse-end placement in a table with empty cells.

usfm-grammar ends a verse at the end of the cell whose text the verse ran out
in. This parser ends a verse at the last position before the next verse starts
(hardening plan D4, `usfm_parser/tests/verse_ends.rs`), which is where the
tcdocs reference files put it in a paragraph and in a table
(`usfmjsTests/usfmBodyTestD/origin.xml` writes `<verse eid="..." /></cell>` in
the last cell of the last row, not after the cell the verse text ended in).
The two rules agree except when empty cells sit between one verse's text and
the next verse's start, which is exactly what this case is about: verse 9a's
end moves to the empty cell before 9b begins, 9b's to the empty cell before
verse 10 begins, and verse 10's to the last cell of the table.

--- origin.xml
+++ origin.xml
@@ -8,20 +8,20 @@
   <para style="b"/>
   <table>
     <row style="tr">
-      <cell style="tc1" align="start"><verse number="9a" style="v" sid="GEN 1:9a"/>test test test <verse eid="GEN 1:9a"/></cell>
+      <cell style="tc1" align="start"><verse number="9a" style="v" sid="GEN 1:9a"/>test test test </cell>
       <cell style="tcr2" align="end"/>
     </row>
     <row style="tr">
-      <cell style="tc1" align="start"/>
+      <cell style="tc1" align="start"><verse eid="GEN 1:9a"/></cell>
       <cell style="tcr2" align="end"><verse number="9b" style="v" sid="GEN 1:9b"/>test again
-<verse eid="GEN 1:9b"/></cell>
+</cell>
     </row>
     <row style="tr">
       <cell style="tc1" align="start"/>
-      <cell style="tcr2" align="end"/>
+      <cell style="tcr2" align="end"><verse eid="GEN 1:9b"/></cell>
     </row>
     <row style="tr">
-      <cell style="tc1" align="start"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="GEN 1:10"/>guol boul 30, silva boul 410 an di res a tingz dem, 1,000, <verse eid="GEN 1:10"/></cell>
+      <cell style="tc1" align="start"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="GEN 1:10"/>guol boul 30, silva boul 410 an di res a tingz dem, 1,000, </cell>
       <cell style="tcr2" align="end"/>
     </row>
     <row style="tr">
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
     </row>
     <row style="tr">
       <cell style="tc1" align="start"/>
-      <cell style="tcr2" align="end"/>
+      <cell style="tcr2" align="end"><verse eid="GEN 1:10"/></cell>
